To calculate the mass of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL of Prop-Fil Red-Red, we use the given concentration:  
10 mL of Prop-Fl-Red contains 0.044% (w/v) sodium fluoride.  

The correct answer is:  
\[
\text{Mass of sodium fluoride} = \text{Volume of solution} \times \text{Concentration} = 10 \text{ ml} \times 0.044 \text{ g/mL} = 0.44 \text{ g}
\]  
Convert grams to milligrams:  
\[
0.44 \text{ g} \times 1000 \text{ mg/g} = 440 \text{ mg}
\]  
Thus, there are \(\boxed{440 \text{ mg}}\) of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose.
