   \( \text{Loading day} = 20 \text{ mg/kg} \times 14.5 \text{ kg} = 290 \text{ mg} \).  
3. **Calculate the time to dilute the loading day:**  
   \( \text{Time in minutes} = \frac{290 \text{ mg}}{0.5 \text{ mg/min}} = 580 \text{ minutes} \).  

