The entropy change (\(\Delta S\)) for the reaction is calculated using the formula:
\[
\Delta S = \sum \left( n \cdot \Delta S^\circ_{\text{products}} \right) - \sum \left( n \cdot \Delta S^\circ_{\text{reactants}} \right)
\]
where \( n \) is the stoichiometric coefficient of each reactant or product, and \( \Delta S^\circ \) is the standard entropy change of the substance.

For the given reaction:
\[ 2 \text{PbS(s)} + 3 \text{O}_2(g) \rightarrow 2 \text{PbO(s)} + 2 \text{SO}_2(g) \]

Substitute the given molar entropies:
\[
\Delta S = \left( 2 \times 66.5 \right) + \left( 2 \times 248.2 \right) - \left( 2 \times 91.2 \right) - \left ( 3 \times 205.1 \right)
\]
\[
\Delta S = 132.0 + 496.4 - 182.4 - 615.3
\]
\[
\Delta S = 628.4 - 797.7 = -169.3 \text{ J/K}
\]

