- \(n_{\text{eff}} - n_f \sim 0.3\), where \(n_{\text{eff}}\) is the effective index of the waveguide, and \(n_f\) is the refractive index of the surrounding film.

The decay length is:

\[
 \text{decay length} = \frac{\lambda_0}{2(n_{\text{eff}} - n_f)}} = \frac{1000 \, \text{nm}}{2 \times 0.3} = 1666 \, \text{nm}
