\[
\lambda_0 / (2n_f)
\]

where:
- \(\lambda_0\) is the wavelength of the incident light,
- \(n_f\) is the refractive of the front (outside) medium.

For a waveguide, the decay length is also given by:

\[
\lambda_0 / (2(n_{\text{guide}} - n_f))
\]

where \(n_{\text{gap}}\) is the refractive index of the waveguide cladding.

For a waveguide, the decay length is:

\[
\lambda_0 / (2(n_{\text{core}} - n_{\text{clad}})
