   - Compute \(R_1^T D R_1\):
     \[
     R_1 = \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\0 & 0 & 1 \end{bmatrix}, \quad R_1^T D R_1 = \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 1 & 1 \\ 1 & 2 & 2 \\ 1 & 2 & 3 \end{bmatrix}, \quad \text{eigenvalue: } 1
     \]
   - The first eigenvalue is \(\lambda_1 = 1\).
   - The first eigenvector is \(\{1, 1, 1\}\).
   - Normalize the eigenvector:
     \[
     \mathbf{v}_1 = \frac{\mathbf{e}_1}{\sqrt{3}} = \begin{bmatrix} 1/\sqrt{3} \\ 1/\sqrt{3} \\ 1/\sqrt{3} \end{bmatrix}.
     \]

